-- **`u64::MAX` in a `static` initialiser -- the eighth of `D3`'s nine slots.**
--
-- `messung/proben/probe-literal-past-the-signed-end.gab` is the regression probe for `D3`,
-- and its own header enumerates the slots the finding covered: *"`return`, `if`, `let`,
-- `static … =`, an assignment, a `bank at`, a `reason` code, an array length, a `walk` node
-- count. One missing character, nine slots."*
--
-- **Seven of those nine were closed on 2026-09-03; this was one of the two that were not.**
-- `instrumente/fuzze-erzeuger.py` printed it at every run afterwards and nobody read the
-- line:
--
--     [==] NICHT-UEBERSETZBAR static-wert              6 of   6
--
-- WHY THE REPAIR DID NOT REACH HERE
-- ---------------------------------
-- `czahl` grew the suffix in the EXPRESSION path -- `ExprArt::Zahl(n)`, the door the user's
-- own number travels through in a `return` or a `let`. A `static` initialiser does not
-- travel that path. The value arrives as an `i128`, out of `konst_zahl` or out of
-- `namen.konstwert`, and was written with `to_string()`:
--
--     static mut x : u64 = 18446744073709551615;
--     ->  static uint64_t x __attribute__((unused)) = 18446744073709551615;
--     cc: integer constant is so large that it is unsigned [-Werror]
--
-- *The `#define` a `const` lowers to had carried a suffix since it was built*, two branches
-- up in the same function. **Two spellings for one thing, and the weaker one decided here**
-- -- `W7`, the shape `konst_wert` had before it.
--
-- WHAT THE FENCE IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT
-- -------------------------------------
-- It takes `czahl`'s boundary and not the `#define`'s. That branch suffixes every
-- non-negative value; `czahl` suffixes only past `2^63 - 1`, for the reason its own note
-- gives: `-Wconversion` and `-Wsign-conversion` read these same literals, so a suffix added
-- where C does not need one trades this error for a different one.
--
-- **Measured rather than argued**: the emitted C of all 613 versioned `.gab` files was
-- dumped before and after, and not one byte moved -- no corpus `static` stands past
-- `2^63 - 1`. A negative value keeps its plain spelling, because `-5u` is not a smaller
-- spelling of `-5` but another number.
--
-- > *Past `2^64 - 1` there is no spelling at all*, and this sink now says so through
-- > `czahl_oder_absage` -- where it used to say *"`static` with a non-constant
-- > initialiser"* about a number that is as constant as a number gets.

module probe::static_past_the_signed_end {

static mut x : u64 = 18446744073709551615;

}
